  "hypothesis": "R38 showed that the existing four-way outcome head cannot act as a selective rescue confidence signal: every locked dual-evidence threshold combination selected zero actions. R39 preserves R37/R38 complete-set ranking, GroupDRO, null option, four-way outcome supervision, selection gate and harm ceiling, while adding one dedicated binary rescue-confidence head per ensemble member. That head is trained directly on rescue-vs-not-rescue terminal labels with inverse-frequency positive weighting and participates in the same stratum-robust objective. Runtime gates on the dedicated binary rescue probability instead of the four-way rescue class probability.",
